<standOff type="notes1" corresp="#TNV8comm3"><note xml:lang="ta" target="#iravular"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 25:</term> kuṟiñcikku… talaimakaṉpeyar cilampaṉ veṟpaṉ poruppaṉ; talaimakaḷpeyar koṭicci kuṟatti…; makkaḷpeyar kuṟavar iṟavuḷar kuṉṟavar.</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#maravar"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 26:</term> pālaikku… talaimakaṉpeyar mīḷi viṭalai kāḷai; talaimakaḷpeyar eyiṟṟi pētai…; makkaḷpeyar eyiṉar eyiṟṟiyar maṟavar maṟattiyar</note>  
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#ayar"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 26–27:</term> mullaikku…  talaimakaṉpeyar kuṟumpoṟaināṭaṉ; talaimakaḷpeyar kiḻatti maṉaivi…; makkaḷpeyar iṭaiyar iṭaicciyar āyar āycciyar.</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#kataiciyar"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 27:</term> marutattukku… talaimakaṉpeyar ūraṉ makiṇaṉ; talaimakaḷpeyar kiḻatti maṉaivi…; makkaḷpeyar kaṭaiyar kaṭaicciyar uḻavar uḻattiyar.</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#nulaicciyar"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 25–26:</term> neytaṟku… talaimakaṉpeyar tuṟaivaṉ koṇkaṉ cērppaṉ; talaimakaḷpeyar nuḷaicci paratti…; makkaḷpeyar paratar parattiyar nuḷaiyar nuḷaicciyar.</note></standOff>
<standOff type="notes4" corresp="#TNV8comm3"><note xml:lang="en" target="#nulaicciyar">Most, but not all, of the designations listed here are found in Caṅkam poetry. Many of the others can be found in the <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">nikantu</hi></term>-s: see <foreign xml:lang="ta-Latn">Tivākaram</foreign> 2.125–140 for a roughly contemporaneous enumeration of the people found in the different poetic settings. I have not presented it here because of its length.</note>
<note xml:lang="en" target="#mili">The TNV here deviates from the IAC, which is otherwise almost identical to it in content. <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">mīḷi</hi></q> is designated as a <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">mullai</hi></term> person, whereas in the IAC, Nakkīrar includes it in his section on <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">pālai</hi></term>.</note>
<note xml:lang="en" target="#manaivi">In IAC 1, p. 26–27, Nakkīrar notes that the <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">talaimakaḷ peyar</hi></q> (‘the names of the women’) <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">kiḻatti</hi></q> and <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">maṉaivi</hi></q> are suitable for <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">mullai</hi></term> and <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">marutam</hi></term>, whereas in the TNV they belong to <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">marutam</hi></term> alone.</note></standOff>
